The classical proof (Ramanujan 1919) uses:
1. Frobenius mod 5: `(1 - X^k)^5 = 1 - X^{5k}` in `(ZMod 5)⟦X⟧`.
2. `(q;q)∞^4 ≡ (q^5;q^5)∞ · J(q) (mod 5)` where `J = 1/(q;q)∞`.
3. Jacobi's identity for `(q;q)∞^3`.
