Define a power series operation `subXPow p f` that sends `∑ aₙ Xⁿ` to `∑ aₙ X^{pn}`.
This is the "raise the variable" map, central to Ramanujan's argument:
in `(ZMod p)⟦X⟧`, `(q;q)∞^p = (q^p; q^p)∞`. -/

